href "/athletes/134833"} "Shinobu Ota"] ", followed by a loss to " [:a {:href "/athletes/126721"} "Almat Kebispayev"] " of Kazakhstan in the repêchage round, putting an end to his campaign."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It was the Cuban, Borrero Molina who dominated Ota, the 2014 Asian Games silver medalist, 8-0 in the gold medal final, giving Cuba their first gold medal of the Rio Games.\nFor the bronze medals, Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117159"} "Stig André Berge"] ", the 2014 World Championships bronze medalist, and three-time Olympian, beat " [:a {:href "/athletes/117135"} "Rövşən Bayramov"] " of Azerbaijan - the World and twice European champion, and two-time Olympic silver medalist. The medal was Norway’s first Olympic wrestling medal in 24 years since " [:a {:href "/athletes/59525"} "Jon Rønningen"] " (NOR) won the gold medal in 52 kg at Barcelona in 1992."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the other bronze medal bout, Uzbekistan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/124125"} "Elmurat Tasmuradov"] " (twice World bronze medalist) had a four-point throw in the last 90 seconds to beat 2012 Olympian " [:a {:href "/athletes/125112"} "Arsen Eraliyev"] " of Kyrgyzstan 13-8 – only the second Olympic Games medal in Greco-Roman for Uzbekistan after " [:a {:href "/athletes/107633"} "Aleksandr Dokturishvili"] " won gold in 74 kg at Athens 2004."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement 